{
	title: 'Noninterrupting /plugin-sync review session and discrepancy indicator',
	spec: `/plugin-sync opens or focuses a dedicated scripted hal/plugin-sync session for the invoking terminal's client/host pair, using no provider or tokens. Startup comparison (task zh7) never switches focus or opens a modal: normal startup lands where the user expects. A persistent compact terminal status indicator says Plugins differ (N) — /plugin-sync until discrepancies are resolved or ignored. Announce newly discovered discrepancies through the existing notice line/stack without permanently crowding out errors. Reconnection or repeated detection does not duplicate notices, sessions or questions. Opening the review is an explicit user action; subsequent changes update it without stealing focus. Existing history and question mechanisms render the scripted session; no new dialog framework.

For each differing portable plugin the intro says how the copies relate: <name> has a newer <file> and the other has not changed it since they last matched; it changed on both computers (or differs without shared history, for config.ason) and the changes merge cleanly or conflict in N places (config.ason: names each setting both changed, with both values); or the copies share no history. Then each side as its name and role (<client hostname without domain> (this computer); <host> (server)) and when it changed, in the shared timestamp format. When both changed it, Hal merges three-way from their nearest common version (git merge-file); config.ason merges per setting instead, also without a common version: a setting changed on one side only takes that change (so a setting on one side only is kept, and one removed on one side stays removed), and settings changed differently on both conflict. A clean merge is offered first and preselected as Use both changes (local +2, server +4 -3). Otherwise offer Use server (+4 -3), drop local changes (+2) and Use local (+2), drop server changes (+4 -3), naming only the sides that changed. On conflict, both copies are written beside the file (<file>.local, <file>.server) and I merged it myself sends the file as it is then; settling removes the copies. Every question ends with Not now (skips the file until the next /sync; Escape answers it, hint Escape: skip question) and Never sync <file> on <client> (the client's .syncignore). When nothing is left, the review names the files the server never syncs and asks whether to sync again any file this client never syncs (Done ends it), so that choice stays visible and reversible. Show no version ids or ancestry jargon. Write for someone who never used a sync tool: never make the user work out a diff direction. When only one side has it, show no diff: say which side has it and whether the other deleted it or never had it, offer Copy to <host> or Copy here and Delete here or Delete on <host>, and preselect the copy. Each option carries its outcome (form choice outcomes), shown live under the options as the selection moves: which computer's file changes, a legend (+ line added on <name>, - line removed from <name>) and the diff of that change, or for one-sided files what is copied or deleted where. Preselect from ancestry, never from clocks: the newer side when only one changed, else Not now. Missing and empty files remain distinct. Not now writes, deletes and ignores nothing; the discrepancy remains discoverable. Never sync uses task zh7's client-side .syncignore policy. Recheck versions when answered and show a revised comparison if either side changed. Report success only after the destination acknowledges the applied update; lifecycle notices follow task b66. Disconnected endpoints cannot complete a pending transfer; show why and allow review after reconnect.

This is a terminal feature. Web gets a discrepancy indicator only if existing shared code supplies it with zero additional work; add no web-specific UI, features or exceptions. Keep config sync and automation deferred. Demonstrate the end-to-end flow with portable keybinding overrides and two different shipped theme selections (task 4c1), including keeping them separate; do not commit real user settings. Verify no startup focus theft with many tabs, discoverability from another tab, Esc deferral, repeat-command focus, ignored-file removal from the count and stale-answer refresh.`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"Wiring: /plugin-sync is a host command, not clientOnly, because sessions, forms, tabs and focus (the go event) live on the host; the remote terminal owns only the comparison and file writes. host/plugin-sync-session.ts finds the typing connection through clients.state.senders and its home through pluginSync.state.followers (now a Map of client to the home its inventory named), opens or reopens one tab per client home named Plugin sync <first 6 hex of the home id> with model hal/plugin-sync, and starts its turn unless a turn or question is under way. The scripted model relays each turn to that home's connected terminal as a plugin-sync event { review: session, answers? }; the terminal (host/plugin-sync-review.ts, wired by main.remote) applies the answer, recompares and replies with a plugin-sync step command { session, say, ask? } checked by common/plugin-sync.ts (forms.invalid). The step is said at once, not typed out: a diff is too long to pace.",
		"turns.runTurn reads a scripted reply's ask, pause and after when its round ends rather than when the model is called, so a stream may settle them while it runs; the relay sets ask after the terminal answers.",
		"Escape pauses the host turn and closes the question, so the terminal hears nothing and writes nothing. A relay wait ends on Escape (the turn's abort signal) or, with the reason said, when no terminal of that home is connected at a checkMs (5 s) check. Session bindings are host memory: after a host restart /plugin-sync binds the tab again. The terminal remembers per session the file and version ids it last asked about; after a terminal restart an answer is not applied and the current comparison is asked instead. Without a later timestamp, Keep separate is preselected: it changes neither plugin file.",
		'Indicator: appView.state.plugins, shown by status-row as the right group after advisories in the warning color, so it is dropped last after them. Notices: one per newly seen (file, client id, server id), key plugin-sync, so reconnects and repeated comparisons add none. The web shows no indicator: no shared code supplies one.',
		'Invariant: a file present on one side only is asked as copy or delete with no diff, and deletion is never preselected. An all-plus diff with "Use server version" preselected deleted a plugin on review (restored from history).',
		'Superseded notes: Escape now skips (form skip; the restarted turn arrives with no answer while a question is remembered, so the terminal answers Not now) and Not now, not Keep separate, is the fallback preselection. The offline version flag (gev) was dropped: nothing but a display label read it. Timestamps use common/titles.ts time(), shared with card headers.',
		'config.ason is compared in sorted key order (config-sync view), so a setting that only moved shows no diff. The sync question has no note about non-portable settings: they never change, so mentioning them only confused.'
	],
	needs: ['zh7', '4c1', 'b66', 'ty', 'w4'],
